{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-mixed-demo-review", "file": "references/seed-motif-generator-checkpoint.md", "content": "# Seed-motif generator checkpoint after a wrong submission

A salient colored seed embedded in a noisy grid does not by itself imply a copy rule. Candidate classes can include translated shape occurrences, periodic/lattice replication, directional rays, or combinations. Before extrapolating, record the seed's exact coordinates and the complete input/output difference mask in every demo. Verify both positive and negative cases: why each changed cell is selected, and why visually similar unchanged cells are excluded. Check palettes and dimensions that vary across demos; distinguish the seed color, target/background color, and unrelated noise empirically rather than assuming one role from a single pair.

After an incorrect submission, discard the whole generator. Do not move a few cells, swap a presumed background color, or switch to a nearby geometric interpretation without replaying it against every demo. With a costly attempt budget, use remaining demos for explicit competing hypotheses and only submit after a full-mask validation. Preserve all cells outside the supported transformation and verify dimensions/row lengths.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u059/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-mixed-demo-review/references/seed-motif-generator-checkpoint.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-mixed-demo-review", "file": "references/cellwise-mask-and-generator-validation.md", "content": "# Cellwise mask validation across heterogeneous demos

When an ARC task has a distinctive colored seed in noisy grids, do not equate resemblance with the rule. Track the seed shape, eligible target values, and spatial generator as independent hypotheses. For every demo, enumerate the full input/output difference mask and preserve negative evidence: unchanged lookalikes, untouched target-valued cells, and the original seed.

Before another demo or a submission, replay the proposed generator against every pair, especially when seed shape, palette, or dimensions vary. A literal translated-template matcher that looks plausible on one example but fails the varied demos is falsified; do not patch it by shifting a few cells. Request additional examples only for explicit remaining alternatives and a specific discriminating observation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u059/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-mixed-demo-review/references/cellwise-mask-and-generator-validation.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-error-recovery", "file": "references/local-demo-global-rule.md", "content": "# Separating a demo's local effect from its global rule

A minimal example may reveal what happens to particular cells without proving how those cells are selected in larger grids. In this session, the 2×10 pair established that a trailing run of 9s becomes 8s and that part of a run remains unchanged, but it did not validate a whole-grid operation for a separate 22×25 test. The first submission simply erased the test's 1-cells; rejection falsified that extrapolation. The next submission erased all test marks except an isolated vertical pair, without a demonstration supporting that selection, and was also unsupported.

When demo and test scales differ sharply, separate and validate: (1) local value mapping, (2) trigger/selection, (3) propagation or geometry, and (4) scope. Keep unchanged demo cells as constraints. If multiple global generators still fit, request a demo designed to distinguish them rather than submitting a conjecture. Never infer an exception mask solely from a visually salient test pattern.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u059/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-error-recovery/references/local-demo-global-rule.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-error-recovery", "file": "references/multi-rejection-demo-discipline.md", "content": "# Multi-rejection discipline for demo-driven ARC

In a task with one or more incorrect submissions, an incorrect result falsifies the whole proposed generator. Do not resubmit a near-identical grid or make an evidence-free palette/coordinate tweak. Rebuild a ledger from every input-output pair, including unchanged cells, and separately test scope, geometry, mapping, and palette.

When multiple candidate grids have failed and the remaining evidence does not determine the test output, stop guessing. State internally at least two concrete hypotheses and the specific observation that distinguishes them. Request one demo only if it can supply that observation, then integrate it before the next action; never treat receiving a demo as an automatic reason for another request. Submit only when one candidate explains every pair and unambiguously yields the test grid. Keep each turn to one action-only JSON object.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u059/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-error-recovery/references/multi-rejection-demo-discipline.md"}
